{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CfbpBUcBTVqFvetBoLUoN", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "First install the dev dependencies, then use pytest. The Makefile wraps it.\n\n```bash\npip install -e .[dev]\nmake test         # runs pytest -q, the whole suite\n```\n\n**`make test-fast` doesn't skip anything right now.** It runs `pytest -m \"not postgres\"`, but no test uses a `postgres` marker. The only slow test is `tests/test_payments.py`, which is marked `@pytest.mark.integration` and sends real requests to an external payments sandbox (`https://sandbox.payments.example`). That test gets skipped only if you exclude the `integration` marker:\n\n```bash\npytest -m \"not integration\" -q   # unit tests only (currently just tests/test_tax.py)\n```\n\nYou'll probably also see an \"unknown marker\" warning, because `integration` isn't registered in `pyproject.toml`.\n\nThe project's EngramDB memory says the slow tests need Postgres and that you should run `docker compose up db` first. That doesn't match the repo: there's no compose file and no Postgres-marked tests. I've flagged that memory as challenged so it gets reviewed.\n\nI haven't run any tests, since the integration test makes network calls to an outside service. If you want, I can change `test-fast` in the Makefile to `-m \"not integration\"` and register the marker."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 700, "cache_read_input_tokens": 25564, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 700}, "output_tokens": 3, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "7ae417e8-3974-4289-b824-395f496645a2", "uuid": "bb1770a1-b52b-4d22-a1ae-cfddfae60919", "timesta